From c32a1e1a71668e13859a67c47056a07d76486b42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:58:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 172/172] media: amlogic: amvdec: allow cache hints on the
 CAPTURE queue

Software deinterlacing or any other CPU access to decoded frames reads
from uncached memory, which caps 1080i MPEG-2 read-back on GXM at 35
fps. Set allow_cache_hints so userspace can request non-coherent
CAPTURE buffers and skip cache maintenance for frames that only go to
the display.

On VIM2 (GXM) with FFmpeg requesting non-coherent buffers and queueing
them with the no-cache-clean and no-cache-invalidate hints:

  1080i MPEG-2 decode + hwdownload: 35 fps -> 90 fps
  576i MPEG-2 decode + hwdownload:  165 fps -> 342 fps
  decode-only 1080i/576i/4K HEVC:   unchanged
  300-frame checksums:              identical

Coherent buffers remain the default.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec.c
index 700f63534232..7491cc406278 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec.c
@@ -948,6 +948,7 @@ static int m2m_queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq,
 	 */
 	dst_vq->gfp_flags = __GFP_NOWARN;
 	dst_vq->io_modes = VB2_MMAP | VB2_DMABUF;
+	dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	dst_vq->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_COPY;
 	dst_vq->ops = &vdec_vb2_ops;
 	dst_vq->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
